Spare Kit geometry kernel: notices
==================================

The geometry kernel (projects/engines/geometry) is Spare Kit's own work under the Mozilla Public
License 2.0 (LICENSE at the repository root), except where a file says it is ported from an
outside source. This file holds the licence text of every outside source the kernel takes code
from, and the credit owed to each, as rule 4 of section 29.20 of the kernel's architecture
(chapter 29, sources and licences) requires. It ships with every binary built from the kernel.

Each entry gives the source's name, how the kernel takes it (section 29.1), its link pinned to a
commit, its licence as the source states it, the kernel files that take from it with the origin
files each comes from, the origin's copyright lines copied exactly, any further credit, and the
licence text in full. Each ported file also starts with its origin files' notices in full.

The notices of the crates compiled into a shipped binary, such as libm, are not kept here: they
go in the generated third-party notices file (rule 4).


